# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
# vendor/

# Go workspace file
#
# go.work is COMMITTED here, deliberately, against the usual advice. The usual
# advice assumes a workspace is one developer's local convenience; this one is
# load-bearing. The root module names the cleat/ SDK nowhere in its go.mod --
# no require, no replace, because `go install pkg@version` refuses a module
# with a replace and the CLIs are meant to be installable that way -- so
# go.work is the only thing that supplies the SDK to the root module's test
# fixtures under testdata/. Without it checked in, a fresh clone cannot run the
# root module's tests at all. See the file's own header.
#
# go.work.sum stays ignored: it is derived, and `go work sync` regenerates it.
go.work.sum

# env file
.env

